  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Quasi-isodynamic (QI) 4-field-period stellarator optimization can achieve Q > 40 with 800 MW fusion at R = 12.5 m, A = 10",
      "REBCO HTS tape can be wound onto complex 3D non-planar modular coil forms without exceeding bending strain limits at Infinity Two scale",
      "TBR = 1.30 is achievable with HCPB blanket conformed to non-axisymmetric stellarator first wall (confirmed by OpenMC with 300M particle histories)",
      "Island divertor (classical W7-X heritage or novel LIBD) can adequately exhaust helium ash over 2-year continuous operating cycles",
      "2-year operating cycle with 30-day planned maintenance outages can deliver high capacity factor (~96% theoretical max)",
      "Inherent stellarator steady-state operation (no plasma current, no disruptions, no ELMs) eliminates entire categories of tokamak risk",
      "Staged Infinity One (2029) → Infinity Two (mid-2030s) validation pathway resolves stellarator physics uncertainties before pilot plant construction"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No central solenoid (eliminates a major capital item present in tokamaks)",
      "No current drive system capital or O&M cost (stellarators are inherently steady-state)",
      "No disruption management system or disruption damage repair O&M (no plasma current to disrupt)",
      "No thermal energy storage / thermal buffering for BOP (constant thermal output, unlike pulsed concepts)",
      "No niobium-based superconductor supply chain dependency (REBCO HTS throughout, unlike LTS stellarators)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "3D non-planar HTS modular coil winding — no manufacturing cost precedent at any scale; dominant LCOE driver (elasticity +0.99)",
      "Island divertor system (classical or LIBD) with complex 3D target geometry, high steady-state heat flux, and no commercial supply chain",
      "HCPB blanket modules conforming to non-axisymmetric stellarator first wall (higher manufacturing cost than axisymmetric tokamak modules)",
      "Potential error field correction coils if manufacturing-scale field errors exceed design tolerance (unbudgeted CAS22 capital)",
      "Large absolute machine scale (R = 12.5 m, ~2× ITER) drives high capital for vessel, building, and coil systems"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "3D HTS coil manufacturing has no cost precedent and no demonstrated industrial process; framework default C220103 ($2.3B) is likely a significant underestimate (3–5× plausible bracket pushes LCOE to 573–840 $/MWh)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Capacity factor is unconstrained by data; 2-year cycle gives 96% theoretical max but actual unplanned outages from ECRH, tritium systems, or divertor degradation could drive availability to 80% (LCOE elasticity −0.93)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Island divertor design choice (classical TRL 4–5 with marginal 0.44–2.9% exhaust efficiency vs. LIBD TRL 2–3 with unvalidated 12.6% efficiency) is deferred to Infinity One results — both options carry capital and availability risk",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Construction schedule overrun likely given 3D HTS coil manufacturing complexity and large machine scale (elasticity +0.55); mid-2030s deployment target highly aggressive",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Li-6 enrichment supply for HCPB pebbles effectively zero in West (COLEX banned under Minamata Convention; ICOMAX decades from scale) — creates geopolitical dependency on Russia/China or requires natural lithium blanket redesign",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium startup procurement (~1 kg at >$35,000/g) coincides with Pearson-projected ~2035 stockpile drawdown from ITER/STEP/CFETR demand — both price and availability may degrade during Infinity Two deployment window",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Thermal efficiency unconfirmed; only published bound is 'Rankine with reheat > 30%' while power balance implies ~45% (would require supercritical steam or sCO₂ cycle)",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape demand of 5,000–15,000 km strains global production capacity (few thousand km/year); current pricing $30–100/kA-m vs. $10/kA-m commercial viability target",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "HCPB blanket integration to non-axisymmetric stellarator first wall is unvalidated; beryllium multiplier is toxic with constrained single-source US supply (Materion)",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Error field correction coils may be required at manufacturing scale despite design intent to avoid them (W7-X required them); unbudgeted capital with no published cost estimate",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Remote maintenance for non-axisymmetric stellarator geometry has no validated tooling (no standard cask or central solenoid removal pathway as in tokamaks); 30-day outage scope undisclosed",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium extraction efficiency over 2-year continuous HCPB operation is untested; any breeding or extraction shortfall cannot be corrected until scheduled outage",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Regulatory pathway uncertain; Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× building cost factor for fission-style regulation is upper bound applicable to all D-T MFE",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
